WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.273
Most teams run their LLM stack across

2
00:00:03.319 --> 00:00:04.446
three or four tools.

3
00:00:04.736 --> 00:00:06.245
The prompt sits in the code.

4
00:00:06.361 --> 00:00:09.055
The traces sit somewhere else, and the bill arrives

5
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.204
from a third place.

6
00:00:10.831 --> 00:00:13.525
Acrux Core is one platform for all of it,

7
00:00:13.745 --> 00:00:15.812
and every part shares one data model.

8
00:00:16.543 --> 00:00:18.784
Prompts are versioned data instead of strings in your

9
00:00:18.842 --> 00:00:19.341
code.

10
00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:23.173
One gateway endpoint stands in front of every provider,

11
00:00:23.219 --> 00:00:24.380
using your own keys.

12
00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:28.246
Calls are traced, through that gateway or straight from

13
00:00:28.293 --> 00:00:29.106
your own client.

14
00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:32.240
Tools get the same versioning that prompts do.

15
00:00:32.403 --> 00:00:35.631
And evaluation scores a prompt against cases taken from

16
00:00:35.712 --> 00:00:36.594
real traffic.

17
00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:38.208
Here is a real prompt.

18
00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:41.227
Version two is live in production, version one is

19
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.874
still on staging, and moving that pointer needs no

20
00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:44.489
deploy.

21
00:00:45.116 --> 00:00:47.369
Every commit is diffable against the one before it.

22
00:00:47.996 --> 00:00:49.679
Calling it takes one request.

23
00:00:50.074 --> 00:00:52.233
You send the prompt name and the alias, and

24
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.147
the template is rendered on our side, not yours.

25
00:00:55.774 --> 00:00:58.247
The reply carries the cost, the provider and the

26
00:00:58.282 --> 00:00:59.907
trace ID already attached.

27
00:01:00.371 --> 00:01:02.461
Nothing has to be reconciled afterwards.

28
00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:04.075
That trace is already waiting.

29
00:01:04.261 --> 00:01:06.861
It holds the model, the tokens, the cost, the

30
00:01:06.908 --> 00:01:09.648
captured payload, and a link to the exact prompt

31
00:01:09.706 --> 00:01:10.646
version behind it.

32
00:01:11.273 --> 00:01:13.143
The gateway is not required for this.

33
00:01:13.398 --> 00:01:15.325
Here is a LangChain agent that called its own

34
00:01:15.372 --> 00:01:19.064
model client, and sent its spans over OpenTelemetry

35
00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:19.691
instead.

36
00:01:20.225 --> 00:01:22.790
A session ties the separate calls of one run

37
00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:26.309
together, so you replay a whole conversation rather than

38
00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:28.004
hunting one request at a time.

39
00:01:28.631 --> 00:01:30.767
Now the part that pays for itself.

40
00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.865
Every reply here was rated by a person, and

41
00:01:34.912 --> 00:01:37.164
the comment says what the answer should have been.

42
00:01:38.151 --> 00:01:40.206
That comment is the valuable part.

43
00:01:40.937 --> 00:01:43.956
When these rows become a dataset, each comment turns

44
00:01:44.002 --> 00:01:45.825
into that case's own pass rule.

45
00:01:46.452 --> 00:01:49.389
So three complaints are now three test cases.

46
00:01:49.726 --> 00:01:52.350
Each one keeps the message that caused it, next

47
00:01:52.373 --> 00:01:54.405
to the rule the answer has to satisfy.

48
00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:57.539
Then both versions run over all three cases.

49
00:01:57.609 --> 00:01:59.443
The version that was live passed one of them.

50
00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.382
The candidate passed all three.

51
00:02:01.603 --> 00:02:03.774
So production was promoted to version two.

52
00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.816
The alias moved, version one stayed exactly where it

53
00:02:06.862 --> 00:02:09.184
was, and nothing was redeployed.

54
00:02:10.171 --> 00:02:12.110
Spending is capped where the calls happen.

55
00:02:12.737 --> 00:02:15.430
A budget refuses the request once the limit is

56
00:02:15.511 --> 00:02:18.368
reached, for the whole team or for one key.

57
00:02:18.994 --> 00:02:21.305
And all of it is open source under Apache

58
00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.350
two point zero.

59
00:02:22.977 --> 00:02:24.683
You can run the whole platform on your own

60
00:02:24.718 --> 00:02:26.076
database, with your own keys.

61
00:02:26.413 --> 00:02:28.584
One platform, from the first prompt to the trace

62
00:02:28.619 --> 00:02:29.548
it produced.
